.TH GIT-COMMIT-WRAPPED 1
.SH NAME
git-commit-wrapped \- create wrapped Git commit messages for agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git commit-wrapped
[\fB--amend\fR]
[\fB--dry-run\fR]
"\fIarea: title\fR"
["\fIcommit body...\fR" ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-commit-wrapped
builds a commit message from command-line arguments, normalizes the subject,
wraps body paragraphs at 72 columns, writes the message to a temporary file,
and runs
.BR git-commit (1)
with
.BR -F .
.PP
Git discovers this executable as
.BR "git commit-wrapped" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --amend
Forward
.B --amend
to
.BR git-commit (1).
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the generated commit message and do not commit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command usage.
.SH AGENT GUIDANCE
.IP 1. 3
Stage only the files for the completed task.
.IP 2. 3
Run this command instead of
.BR "git commit -m" ,
printf, heredocs, or manual wrapping.
.IP 3. 3
Pass the body as plain text. Do not split lines manually.
.IP 4. 3
The title is lowercased automatically.
.IP 5. 3
If the title is too long, shorten it and run the command again.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
git commit-wrapped "docs: require pre-tag review" \
  "Document the review requirement before release tags. The script wraps this body automatically."

git commit-wrapped --amend "matching: fix candidate ordering" \
  "Preserve deterministic ordering when two candidates have equal rank."
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-commit (1)
